  "solution": {
    "text": "In lsomers of Hydrocarbon heat of combustion depends upon their stability. As stability increases, heat of combustion decreases.<br />trans-alkenes are more stable than cis-alkenes<br />Stability <math><mo>∝</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mtext>&nbsp;of&nbsp;combustion</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math><br />Stability <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></math><br />Heat of combustion <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math>"
  }
